-- title:
--   Original stopped BV discounted full mixed negative-J and Y-Taylor C1 errors vanish together
-- statement:
--   For almost every original bounded-variation Lévy sample path, the actual strict compact-band physical Y Taylor remainder and mixed Y/J commutator both vanish on source-refining stopped grids. The mixed term needs only one inner strict compact segment for actual raw J, thanks to the new strict-margin shift lemma. The result matches the two error terms of the Proved full Stieltjes cash source C1 identity, leaving stopped-path localisation and strict horizon atom accounting explicit.

import Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.ContDiff.Defs
import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Exponential
import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.MeasurableSpace.Defs
import Mathlib.Topology.Order.LeftRightLim
import Definitions.Def_AvramDividend_Classical_SpectrallyNegativeLevy
import Definitions.Def_AvramDividend_Classical_DividendStrategy
